  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1226 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nThe pattern should become much drier for the latter part of this \nweek as the front lifts back to the north.  Upper-level ridging will \nstart building back in across Mexico and southeast Texas starting \nWednesday while troughing will be located over the west coast.\nThis setup will place the region in southwest flow aloft and allow a \nfeed of Pacific moisture into the Panhandle and northwest Texas. \nMost of our forecast area should remain dry and warm with highs in \nthe mid 90s.  However, some low (<20%) chances for showers and \nthunderstorms will continue for the Big Country and western Concho \nValley Wednesday through Friday.  Looking ahead to the weekend, the \nupper-level flow should become quasi zonal again as the ridge starts \nto break down.  Models indicate another cold front potentially \nintruding into Texas over the weekend which would result in low (20-\n30%) chances for rain showers returning to the forecast.\n\nSK",
